# ValueX Firehose (v0)

Autonomous data collection, scoring, and routing for implicit demand using public signals only. No landing pages.

- Sources: Reddit, X (snscrape), HN (Algolia), StackOverflow, GitHub Issues, RSS
- API: Local MVP `/route` at <http://127.0.0.1:8000>
- Outputs:
  - NDJSON events: `data/events_YYYYMMDD.ndjson`
  - Leads CSV: `data/leads.csv`
  - Outreach drafts: `data/outreach_drafts/YYMMDD/*.txt`
  - Summary: `data/summary_latest.md`

## Quickstart

1. Install deps

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

1. Start API (new terminal)

```bash
uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000
```

1. Run one pass (fetch + score + write)

```bash
python ingest/runner.py
```

1. Optional: QA sampler

```bash
python qa/sample_labeler.py
```

Make targets (optional):

- `make api` → run the API
- `make run` → run ingestion once
- `make sample` → QA sample CSV
- `make daily` → one-shot daily run (cron-friendly)

## Suppression CLI

Basic helpers around the suppression store at `data/suppression.jsonl`.

Examples:

```bash
python scripts/suppression_cli.py check you@example.com
python scripts/suppression_cli.py add you@example.com --reason bounce --source test
python scripts/suppression_cli.py remove you@example.com
python scripts/suppression_cli.py list --head 5
```

## Mailer (dryrun/live)

Simple SMTP sender with suppression awareness and List-Unsubscribe headers.

1) Configure env (see `.env.example`):

```
SENDER_DOMAIN=example.com
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com   # or Brevo
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=...
SMTP_PASS=...
SMTP_FROM=no-reply@example.com
SMTP_NAME=ValueX
UNSUBSCRIBE_ADDRESS=unsubscribe@example.com
UNSUBSCRIBE_URL=https://example.com/unsub?e={email}
```

2) Dryrun (writes `.eml` to `data/outbox/`):

```bash
python scripts/send_cli.py you@example.com "Hello" "<p>Hi there</p>"
```

3) Live send (requires SMTP vars):

```bash
python scripts/send_cli.py you@example.com "Hello" "<p>Hi there</p>" --live
```

Notes:

- Suppressed recipients are skipped with `{ ok: true, suppressed: true }`.
- List-Unsubscribe headers are added automatically when UNSUBSCRIBE_* vars are set.
